  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Mean \\(\\bar{x}=\\frac{\\sum x}{n}\\) or \\(\\Sigma x=n \\bar{x}\\)\n\\(\\Sigma \\mathrm{x}=25 \\times 78.4=1960\\)\nBut this \\(\\Sigma \\mathrm{x}\\) is incorrect as 96 was misread as 69 .\n\\(\\begin{aligned}\n& \\therefore \\text { correct } \\Sigma \\mathrm{x}=1960+(96-69)=1987 \\\\\n& \\therefore \\text { correct mean }=\\frac{1987}{25}=79.48\n\\end{aligned}\\)",
    "image": null
  },
